{
  "case_id": "2019-18-280",
  "document_hash": "2a517d3de29f82b292990285d4767b741d8f78012492da012ceb40a0f1d896c8",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-280",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2a517d3de29f82b292990285d4767b741d8f78012492da012ceb40a0f1d896c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2a517d3de29f-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "PAUL D. CLEMENT, ESQ., Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioners.\nJEFFREY B. WALL, Principal Deputy Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Petitioners.\nRICHARD P. DEARING, ESQ., New York, New York; on behalf of the Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2019-18-280",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2a517d3de29f82b292990285d4767b741d8f78012492da012ceb40a0f1d896c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2a517d3de29f-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CLEMENT: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court:\nText, history, and tradition all make clear that New York City's restrictive premises license and accompanying transport ban are unconstitutional. The city's restriction on transporting firearms to places where they may be lawfully possessed and its insistence in its revised regulations that any such transport be continuous and uninterrupted are premised on a view of the Second Amendment as a home-bound right, with any ability to venture beyond the curtilage with a firearm, even locked and unloaded, a matter of government grace.\nThat view is inconsistent with text, history, tradition, and this Court's cases."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-280",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2a517d3de29f82b292990285d4767b741d8f78012492da012ceb40a0f1d896c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2a517d3de29f-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But, Mr. -- Mr. Clement, the city has now been blocked by a state law, and the state has not been party to these proceedings. The state says: City, thou shalt not enforce the regulations. So what's left of this case? The Petitioners have gotten all the relief that they sought. They can carry a gun to a second home. They can carry it to a fire -- to a practice range out of state."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-280",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2a517d3de29f82b292990285d4767b741d8f78012492da012ceb40a0f1d896c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2a517d3de29f-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I thought that\nthat's the representation they made to this\nCourt."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-280",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2a517d3de29f82b292990285d4767b741d8f78012492da012ceb40a0f1d896c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2a517d3de29f-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: No, Mr. Clement,\nwhat you're asking us to do is to take a case in which the other side has thrown in the towel and completely given you every single thing you demanded in your complaint for relief, and you're asking us to opine on a law that's not on the books anymore, and one that's not on the books, not because of something necessarily the city did but because the state, a party who's not a party to this litigation, has changed the law and prohibited them from doing.\nSo this is, I think, something quite\ndifferent. You're asking us to opine on an old\nlaw, not the new law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-280",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2a517d3de29f82b292990285d4767b741d8f78012492da012ceb40a0f1d896c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2a517d3de29f-0000-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I'm sorry, that --\nthat's the oddest decision I've heard. Answer\nan old law that's no longer in effect and then\nreserve consideration of the new law's\ninterpretation for the lower courts? I don't\nknow how that doesn't constitute mootness on the\nissue that's before us."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2019-18-280",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2a517d3de29f82b292990285d4767b741d8f78012492da012ceb40a0f1d896c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2a517d3de29f-0000-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: I probably have a --\nMR. CLEMENT: -- to have --\nJUSTICE BREYER: I mean, I don't think\nit's bad when people who have an argument settle\ntheir argument and, thus, there no longer is\none, so I wonder if -- should I ask them this\nquestion? You say this case is still alive\nbecause the City of New York might prosecute one\nof your clients because they stopped for coffee\non the way to a firing range.\nI think I'm going to ask them that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2019-18-280",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2a517d3de29f82b292990285d4767b741d8f78012492da012ceb40a0f1d896c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2a517d3de29f-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "On mootness, Petitioners pointed below to economic harms from the violation of their constitutional rights."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-280",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2a517d3de29f82b292990285d4767b741d8f78012492da012ceb40a0f1d896c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2a517d3de29f-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But they never asked for it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Wall",
      "case_id": "2019-18-280",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2a517d3de29f82b292990285d4767b741d8f78012492da012ceb40a0f1d896c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2a517d3de29f-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. WALL: That's true, Justice Ginsburg, but there's a specific federal rule on this, Federal Rule 54(c), which says the prayer of relief binds on a default judgment, but it doesn't bind when you've litigated on the merits."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-280",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2a517d3de29f82b292990285d4767b741d8f78012492da012ceb40a0f1d896c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2a517d3de29f-0001-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Such bans have been rare and commonly struck down precisely because the right to keep arms and keep and bear arms must entail and has always entailed the ability of a law-abiding citizen to carry a firearm unloaded and locked from one lawful place to another."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-18-280",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2a517d3de29f82b292990285d4767b741d8f78012492da012ceb40a0f1d896c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2a517d3de29f-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They filed a complaint. They filed a motion for summary judgment. They briefed this case before the Second Circuit. They filed a cert petition. Then, in response to the suggestion of mootness, they filed another brief there."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Richard P. Dearing",
      "case_id": "2019-18-280",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2a517d3de29f82b292990285d4767b741d8f78012492da012ceb40a0f1d896c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2a517d3de29f-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF RICHARD P. DEARING ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENTS"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-280",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "2a517d3de29f82b292990285d4767b741d8f78012492da012ceb40a0f1d896c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2a517d3de29f-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: You're just not going to prosecute them for any violation of this old law?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-18-280",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "2a517d3de29f82b292990285d4767b741d8f78012492da012ceb40a0f1d896c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2a517d3de29f-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Mr. Dearing, are the -- are people in New York less safe now as a result of the enactment of the new city and state laws than they were before?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2019-18-280",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "2a517d3de29f82b292990285d4767b741d8f78012492da012ceb40a0f1d896c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2a517d3de29f-0002-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "city stays safe."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2019-18-280",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "2a517d3de29f82b292990285d4767b741d8f78012492da012ceb40a0f1d896c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2a517d3de29f-0002-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Two -- two are in Staten Island."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2019-18-280",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2a517d3de29f82b292990285d4767b741d8f78012492da012ceb40a0f1d896c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2a517d3de29f-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The claim in this case was specifically articulated by the Petitioners that they have a premises license, this is about the scope of a premises license, and the claim made framed by the Petitioners most clearly in their summary judgment papers at page 6 was that the relief sought here is necessary to allow the full exercise of the -- of the right of defense of hearth and home in the home."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2019-18-280",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2a517d3de29f82b292990285d4767b741d8f78012492da012ceb40a0f1d896c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2a517d3de29f-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: I just want to circle back to the direct and continuous travel requirement of the current rule and Justice Alito's question about visiting your mother. Is it now the city's position that any reasonable stops are permissible?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2019-18-280",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2a517d3de29f82b292990285d4767b741d8f78012492da012ceb40a0f1d896c8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2a517d3de29f-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Get a cup of coffee? I mean, I'm not sure a cup --is a cup of coffee reasonably necessary?"
    },
